## Sluice

::bg{location="library" time="night"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Three brass wheels stand in the wall below a door of green bronze. Each is stamped with a sea-creature: an eel, a gull, a crown.
@quill{code="0010" os when="entry.quillFirst.everRead"}: The librarians used to open it at low tide. Low things first, they said.

<branch id="valveOrder" prompt="Which wheel first?">
  <choice id="eelFirst" text="The eel, then the gull, then the crown">
    ::set{run.valves += 3}
    @narrator{code="0020"}: The wheels turn one after another. Somewhere behind the bronze, water drains away with a long sigh.
    ::assert{solved(sluice)}
    @ilo{code="0010" mono}: Low things first.
  </choice>
  <choice id="crownFirst" text="The crown first">
    ::set{run.valves += 1}
    @narrator{code="0030"}: The crown wheel spins free and the corridor floods to the ceiling. Ilo claws his way back to the stair.
  </choice>
  <choice id="gullFirst" text="The gull first">
    ::set{run.valves += 1}
    @narrator{code="0040"}: The gull wheel will not move. Something behind the door laughs, very quietly.
  </choice>
</branch>
